<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Guided Sahlenburg–Neuwerk Wadden crossing — Guided Sahlenburg–Neuwerk historical mapped planning course [planning only — not navigation-grade]</name><desc>Book an authorised guide for the tidal crossing from Sahlenburg beach near Cuxhaven to Neuwerk. Confirm the rescue-station meeting at Hans-Claußen-Straße 18 and arrange island exploration and return transport separately; Duhnen is a different departure. Never walk independently or navigate by the historical map. Dangerous tides, channels, mud, cold water, fog and storms mean the guide chooses the safe course and can cancel. Children must be eight or older, with an adult for under-fourteens; the guide assesses fitness for long uneven walking and water crossings. Wear firm-soled shoes and socks, not bare feet, sandals, soft water booties or Beachies; gumboots are unsuitable. Bring warm weatherproof clothing, leash dogs and protect wildlife. Any unavailable required leg prevents the whole itinerary. Operator estimates of 10 km and 210 minutes vary with conditions; the historical mapped line is about 8.9 km.

Historical planning geometry: © OpenStreetMap contributors — https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright. Open Database License 1.0: https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1.0/. The main tidal alignment dates from March 2021, and the tidal course can change each year. It is not a current field survey or a safe independent navigation route. Planning only; not navigation-grade.

